Per ES spec UpdateEmpty semantics, compound statements always produce a
completion value. Reset eval_acc_reg to undefined at the entry of if-statements
(since even a not-taken or empty branch returns NormalCompletion(undefined), not
EMPTY) and before/per-iteration in while, do-while, and for-of loops (V starts
as undefined; empty-body or zero-iteration cases must not leak prior values).

Fixes all 18 cptn-value test262 failures:
  language/statements/if/cptn-{else-false-nrml,else-true-nrml,no-else-true-nrml,
    else-true-abrupt-empty,else-false-abrupt-empty,no-else-true-abrupt-empty,
    no-else-false}
  language/statements/while/cptn-{no-iter,abrupt-empty,iter}
  language/statements/do-while/cptn-{normal,abrupt-empty}
  language/statements/for-of/cptn-{decl-no-itr,decl-itr,decl-abrupt-empty,
    expr-itr,expr-no-itr,expr-abrupt-empty}

quick.sh: 283 pass / 0 fail (unchanged).

